# ECaR app context

Exceptions and traps only. Every line was seen in screenshots on 2026-11-23 and has not yet been seen in a run.

- The app runs in its own window with no browser tabs. A second window titled "Launching ECaR" stays behind it. Ignore that window.
- The X at the top right corner of the window closes the whole app. Never click it.
- Tabs inside the page, such as "Account Locator" and "Account Information", have their own small x at the right end of the tab title.
- While the app is working it shows a spinner and "Request in process. Please wait" at the top left. Wait until both are gone.
- An opened account always lands on its "Action Log" sub-tab.
- The account page is taller than the screen. A row of buttons (Edit, Save, Cancel, Payment Information, Balance Details) is at the very bottom. Scroll with the pointer over the middle of the page.
- "Payment Information" opens a separate smaller window with a red "Close" button.
- A red line saying customer authentication is not complete is expected on the Details sub-tab.
- Edit, Save, Edit Note, Request Acct and Search FDR change data or start other work. This app context never needs them.

## Known interruptions

None observed yet.





# Procedure: read five payment values for one ECaR ID and write them back.
schema_version: 1

id: download-payment-details
version: "2026-11-24.1"
persona: ecar-download-payments
description: Read five payment values for one ECaR ID and write them to the request row.

# "reference" holds the ECaR ID, because the queue tool's key column is
# named "reference". The result columns in the CSV are not work-item fields:
# declared fields must be filled, and the result columns start empty.
work_item:
  key: reference
  fields:
    reference: {type: text}

steps:
  # ---- Finding and claiming work -------------------------------------------
  - id: find-request
    role: pickup
    intent: Get the next ECaR ID that nobody has started.
    via: tool
    tool: work_queue_csv.next_item
    when_nothing_found: no_work
    irreversible: false
    on_fail: {retries: 1, then: send_to_human}

  - id: claim-request
    role: claim
    intent: Mark the row as claimed.
    via: tool
    tool: work_queue_csv.mark
    args: {reference: "{reference}", status: claimed}
    irreversible: false
    on_fail: {retries: 1, then: send_to_human}

  # ---- Opening the app and signing on --------------------------------------
  - id: open-ecar
    role: work
    intent: Open ECaR, or bring it to the front if it is already open.
    app: ecar
    via: tool
    tool: launch_app.launch_app
    args: {app: ecar}
    irreversible: false
    on_fail: {retries: 0, then: send_to_human}

  - id: check-sign-on
    role: work
    intent: Look at the ECaR window. Take no action unless the page is blank or still loading; in that case wait.
    app: ecar
    via: screen
    done_when: The window shows either the "Channel Secure Sign On" page or the ECaR main page with its menu bar (Account, Phone, Specialty Processing).
    captures:
      - name: sign_on_showing
        type: text
        allowed_values: ["yes", "no"]
        question: Is the "Channel Secure Sign On" page showing?
        double_read: true
    irreversible: false
    on_fail: {retries: 1, then: send_to_human}

  - id: sign-on
    role: work
    intent: A person signs on by hand.
    app: ecar
    via: tool
    tool: pause_for_human.pause_for_human
    args: {message: "Sign on in the ECaR window yourself, then come back here and press Enter."}
    skip_if: {value: sign_on_showing, compare: equals, to: "no"}
    verify_with: screen
    done_when: The sign-on page is gone and the ECaR main page with its menu bar is showing.
    irreversible: false
    on_fail: {retries: 0, then: send_to_human}

  - id: check-main-page
    role: work
    intent: Look at the ECaR main page. Take no action.
    app: ecar
    via: screen
    done_when: The ECaR main page with its menu bar is showing, with or without a "Status" box on top of it.
    captures:
      - name: environment_is_uat
        type: text
        allowed_values: ["yes", "no"]
        question: Does the title bar at the very top of the window include the text "UAT"?
        double_read: true
      - name: status_box_showing
        type: text
        allowed_values: ["yes", "no"]
        question: Is a box titled "Status" with a "Confirm" button showing on top of the page?
        double_read: true
    rules: [must-be-uat]
    irreversible: false
    on_fail: {retries: 1, then: send_to_human}

  - id: confirm-status
    role: work
    intent: Click the "Confirm" button at the bottom of the "Status" box.
    app: ecar
    via: screen
    skip_if: {value: status_box_showing, compare: equals, to: "no"}
    done_when: No "Status" box is showing and the Account Locator tab is visible with its "ECaR ID" field.
    irreversible: false
    on_fail: {retries: 1, then: send_to_human}

  # ---- Finding the account -------------------------------------------------
  - id: search-account
    role: work
    intent: >
      On the Account Locator tab, click "Clear", type {reference} into the
      "ECaR ID" field under General, and click "Search". If a box titled
      "Customer Authentication" asks "Is this an incoming call?", click "No".
      Wait until the account opens.
    app: ecar
    via: screen
    inputs: [reference]
    done_when: >
      A tab whose title starts with "Account Information" and ends with
      {reference} is open and selected, and no box or spinner is on top of it.
    irreversible: false
    on_fail: {retries: 1, then: send_to_human}
    hints:
      - Search is the first of three buttons. Never click "Search FDR".
      - While a spinner or "Request in process" is showing, wait.
      - If the Results table is still empty after the search finishes, answer cannot_proceed.

  - id: open-details
    role: work
    intent: Click the "Details" sub-tab, the first in the row that also has Contacts, Guarantors and Action Log.
    app: ecar
    via: screen
    done_when: The "Details" sub-tab is selected and shows the "Summary" and "Amount Past Due" sections.
    irreversible: false
    on_fail: {retries: 1, then: send_to_human}

  # ---- Reading the payment details -----------------------------------------
  - id: open-payment-information
    role: work
    intent: Scroll the account page down until the row of buttons at the bottom is visible, then click "Payment Information".
    app: ecar
    via: screen
    done_when: A separate window titled "Payment Information" is in front, with its "Payment Details" tab selected.
    irreversible: false
    on_fail: {retries: 1, then: send_to_human}
    hints:
      - The button row reads Edit, Save, Cancel, Payment Information, Balance Details. Click only "Payment Information".

  - id: read-payment-details
    role: work
    intent: Look at the "Payment Details" tab of the Payment Information window. Take no action.
    app: ecar
    via: screen
    done_when: The Payment Information window is in front with "Payment Details" selected and the label "Current Amount Due" visible.
    captures:
      - name: current_amount_due
        type: text
        question: What does the box next to "Current Amount Due" show, exactly as displayed? If the box is empty, answer BLANK.
        double_read: true
      - name: current_date_due
        type: text
        question: What does the box next to "Current Date Due" show, exactly as displayed? If the box is empty, answer BLANK.
        double_read: true
      - name: fixed_payment_amount
        type: text
        question: What does the box next to "Fixed Payment Amount" show, exactly as displayed? If the box is empty, answer BLANK.
        double_read: true
      - name: current_statement_balance
        type: text
        question: What does the box next to "Current Statement Balance" show, exactly as displayed? If the box is empty, answer BLANK.
        double_read: true
      - name: mail_statement_to
        type: text
        question: What does the box next to "Mail Statement To" show, exactly as displayed? If the box is empty, answer BLANK.
        double_read: true
    irreversible: false
    on_fail: {retries: 1, then: send_to_human}

  # ---- Closing up ----------------------------------------------------------
  - id: close-payment-window
    role: work
    intent: Click the red "Close" button inside the Payment Information window.
    app: ecar
    via: screen
    done_when: No Payment Information window is showing and the ECaR main window is in front with the Account Information tab.
    irreversible: false
    on_fail: {retries: 1, then: send_to_human}

  - id: close-account
    role: work
    intent: Click the small x at the right end of the "Account Information" tab title to close that tab.
    app: ecar
    via: screen
    done_when: The Account Locator tab is selected and no "Account Information" tab is open.
    irreversible: false
    on_fail: {retries: 1, then: send_to_human}
    hints:
      - Never click the X at the top right corner of the window.

  # ---- Finishing -----------------------------------------------------------
  - id: complete-request
    role: complete
    intent: Mark the row completed and write the five values to it.
    via: tool
    tool: work_queue_csv.mark
    args:
      reference: "{reference}"
      status: completed
      columns:
        current_amount_due: "{current_amount_due}"
        current_date_due: "{current_date_due}"
        fixed_payment_amount: "{fixed_payment_amount}"
        current_statement_balance: "{current_statement_balance}"
        mail_statement_to: "{mail_statement_to}"
    irreversible: false
    on_fail: {retries: 1, then: send_to_human}




# Persona: the scope of work for one agent. One persona, one work type.
schema_version: 1

id: ecar-download-payments
name: ECaR download payments
work_type: download-payment-details
description: >
  Looks up one account in ECaR (UAT) by its ECaR ID, reads five values from
  the Payment Details tab, and writes them back to the request row. Read only.

procedure: procedure.yaml
rules: rules.yaml
guardrails: guardrails.yaml

apps: [ecar]
tools: [work_queue_csv, launch_app, pause_for_human, escalate]

polling:
  interval_seconds: 60

models:
  actor: default
  verifier: default
  reader: default

unfit_rule_default: human

escalation:
  tool: escalate
  destination: review_file

# Guidance given to the model. This is not enforcement.
guidance:
  do:
    - Work only on the account whose ECaR ID you were given.
    - Read values exactly as displayed.
  do_not:
    - Do not click Edit, Save, Edit Note, Request Acct or Search FDR.
    - Do not change any field or dropdown other than the ECaR ID search field.
    - Do not answer Yes to "Is this an incoming call?".
